<title>USA: U.S. June retail sales rose 0.5 percent.</title>
<headline>U.S. June retail sales rose 0.5 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on U.S. retail sales.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  June    May-(Prev) June97/96</p>
<p> Retail Sales	    0.5   -0.3  -0.1     3.8</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	 0.3   Unch  -0.1     3.8</p>
<p> Auto Sales		1.1   -1.2  -0.2     3.6</p>
<p> Durable Goods	   0.5   -0.9  -0.3     3.4</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods	0.4    0.1  Unch     4.0</p>
<p> Furniture Stores	1.5    0.5   0.6     6.8</p>
<p> Building Materials   -1.2   -0.1  -0.6     3.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: June     May-(Previous)    Apr--(Prev)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 210.30   209.31  210.16   209.93  210.44</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    159.89   159.46  159.60   159.49  159.77</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    50.41    49.85   50.55    50.45   50.67</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 85.13    84.70   85.75    85.47   86.00</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   125.17   124.61  124.55   124.46  124.52</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.87    11.69   11.65    11.64   11.58</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.91    12.05   11.96    12.07   12.02</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:  June    May-(Prev) June97/96</p>
<p> General Merch.Stores  0.8    0.5   0.7     6.2</p>
<p> Department Stores     0.9    0.5   0.7     7.4</p>
<p> Food Stores	    -0.1    0.1   0.2     2.2</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	 -0.2    0.1   0.1     1.7</p>
<p> Gas Stations	   -0.9   -2.0  -0.7    -2.1</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 Unch    1.2   0.8     0.6</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places	1.1   Unch  -1.0     5.3</p>
<p> Drug Stores	     0.3    0.1   0.2     8.6</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: June     May-(Previous)     Apr----(Prev)</p>
<p> Gen.Merch.Stores    27.54    27.33    27.29     27.20   27.11</p>
<p> Department Stores   21.69    21.50    21.45     21.40   21.30</p>
<p> Food Stores	   35.85    35.87    36.03     35.83   35.97</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	33.73    33.79    33.95     33.77   33.92</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  12.68    12.79    13.03     13.06   13.12</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.60     9.61     9.61	9.49    9.53</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    20.47    20.24    19.89     20.24   20.08</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    8.11     8.08     8.09	8.08    8.07</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected June retail sales to rise 0.2 percent, and sales excluding autos to be up 0.5 percent.</p>
<p>The department revised April retail sales to down 1.1 percent from a previously reported 0.9 percent decline. April retail sales excluding autos were revised to down 0.6 percent from a previously reported 0.5 percent decline.</p>
